{
  "case_id": "2009-09-497",
  "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The agreement between Antonio Jackson and Rent-A-Center should be enforced as written. There is no statutory impediment to the enforcement of the clear and unmistakable agreement that gives the arbitrator exclusive authority to decide Jackson's challenge to enforceability, nor is there any language in the Federal Arbitration Act that would prohibit the court from making the determination -- prohibit the arbitrator from making the determination of Jackson's challenge to unconscionability."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, do you understand -- and we can ask the Respondent. But, as you understand Jackson's case, is he saying that part of the clause, part of the arbitration clause, is unconscionable, that the whole clause is unconscionable or that the whole contract is unconscionable?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He has attacked certain provisions specifically of the agreement. He is arguing about the discovery provision. He is arguing about the fees provision. And he is arguing about certain terms excluding claims, that bilaterally exclude claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you agree that a contract cannot be unconscionable unless it was coerced, that a finding of unconscionability is the same as a finding of coercion? You don't agree with that, do you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Friedman",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "With respect to procedural unconscionability, issues of unequal economic bargaining power, which is essentially what we have here -- those are non-issues that cannot be addressed by the arbitrator."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Silverberg, the section 2 on which you place much emphasis just says that agreements are enforceable save on such grounds as exist in law or equity for revocation of a contract. But the section 2 doesn't say any -- anything about who decides that question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But which is the stronger case for arbitration? Case one, you attack the arbitration clause only, part of the arbitration contract only, as being unconscionable. Case two, you attack the whole agreement as being unconscionable. Do those both stand on the same footing, or is one a stronger case for submission to the court than the other?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Silverberg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think this Court has made clear in the severability cases that challenges to the contract as a whole would go to the arbitrator to decide."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So an attack on the -- as I think Justice Breyer noted, you -- an argument that it's one-sided goes to the entire arbitration agreement. I don't want to arbitrate because that's not what I chose to do freely. Correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Silverberg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That would be the court under our position, Your Honor, and that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chamber of Commerce",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0002-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The amici certainly claim the contrary. The Chamber of Commerce claims that this is what\u2019s happening and that it has been a snowballing effect."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there something unusual about limiting discovery to documents?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right. What is the one-sentence answer, one sentence, to the thing, this is a very interesting case, lots of stuff in it that we needn't reach because irrespective of everything else, they in their reply, the district court, and the court of appeals all said these whole four pages, the whole four pages were unconscionable, so none of it\u2019s enforceable, and all we have to decide is whether that's an issue for the court. And the answer to that being not an issue for the court is what, in a sentence or two?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Friedman",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No, Justice Breyer, the determination of unconscionability is for the arbitrator. The -- the limited role of the court goes only to the making, not to the issue of unconscionability. So the court --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The problem -- I -- I keep going back to my initial question to you, is you want to parse out what making is from unconscionability, and you want us to say, well, if it's too onerous a fee for arbitration, that goes to the making, because you\u2019re depriving the party of -- of an arbitration forum. If it's discovery, that doesn't go to depriving them of anything because the arbitrator could give them more discovery if he or she chose. Am I correct, this is your argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If there\u2019s no access to arbitration, there\u2019s no way that you can leave that issue to the arbitrator, is there?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-09-497",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac1a5cdb9cb565291af52a2f1256869f7e08ace48bc91247d82f881f5da18759",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac1a5cdb9cb5-0003-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:03 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
